    </details>
  </section>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Each complete chunk agrees with the following singular, plural, or uncountable noun and matches the stated positive or negative meaning.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the natural chunk</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read to the noun first. Then choose the chunk that fits.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There’s">There’s</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There are">There are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There isn’t">There isn’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There aren’t">There aren’t</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The map introduces one pharmacy: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="There’s" data-hint="A pharmacy is one countable thing, so use the contracted singular chunk There's." data-fix="There's a pharmacy on the corner." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a pharmacy on the corner.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The building guide lists two elevators: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="There are" data-hint="Two elevators is plural, so use There are." data-fix="There are two elevators in the building." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> two elevators in the building.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The listing says parking is unavailable: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="There isn’t" data-hint="A parking lot is singular, and the sentence states that it is absent." data-fix="There isn't a parking lot, so I take the bus." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a parking lot, so I take the bus.</span></div>
