        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two">two</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="one">one</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three">three</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a parking space" data-hint="The listing uses There isn't before one missing apartment feature." data-fix="There isn't a parking space.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Which listed apartment feature is missing?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a parking space">a parking space</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a kitchen">a kitchen</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a closet">a closet</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="across the street" data-hint="The sentence about the bus stop ends with its location." data-fix="The bus stop is across the street.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Where is the bus stop?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="across the street">across the street</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in the building">in the building</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on the corner">on the corner</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="are there any stores nearby" data-hint="The customer is asking about plural stores, so begin with Are there, then use any." data-fix="Are there any stores nearby?" data-success-message="Correct. The plural question moves are before there and uses any before stores.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">A new resident wants to know whether the area has stores. Build the plural question.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="stores">stores</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="any">any</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">Are</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="nearby">nearby</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="there">there</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="there isn’t an elevator in the building" data-hint="Begin with There isn't because elevator is singular and the inspection found none." data-fix="There isn't an elevator in the building." data-success-message="Correct. The singular negative keeps there first and places isn't before an elevator.">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the negative</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The accessibility inspection found no elevator. Build the singular negative.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="elevator">elevator</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="in">in</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="there">There</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="building">building</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="isn’t">isn’t</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="an">an</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="is" data-hint="Look forward to the noun phrase two bathrooms before choosing is or are." data-fix="There are two bathrooms." data-why="Two bathrooms is plural, so use there are.">
    <h3>Drill 6: the noun decides</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="there">There</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="bathrooms">bathrooms.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="it" data-hint="The caller is introducing the problem for the first time, so no earlier noun gives it a referent." data-fix="There is a problem with my order." data-why="Use there is to introduce a problem. It is needs a known referent from the earlier context.">
    <h3>Drill 7: introduce it with there</h3>
    <p>A caller begins the conversation with “It is a problem with my order.” Tap the word that is wrong in this first mention.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it">It</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="problem">a problem</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="order">with my order.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> There is a chair. Change to three.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There are three chairs.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> There is a parking lot. Make a question.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Is there a parking lot?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> There are some seats. Make it negative.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There aren’t any seats.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Is there a restroom? Answer yes.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Yes, there is.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> Are there any tables? Answer no.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>No, there aren’t.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> My street has a pharmacy. Say it with there’s.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There’s a pharmacy on my street.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to describe your actual home, neighborhood, workplace, location, schedule, or finances. Use an invented map, a fictional listing, or a teacher-read scene card. If a visual is not accessible, the teacher reads every relevant feature aloud.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Apartment card:</b> Give a six-sentence tour of an invented apartment or a provided listing. Include a singular item, a plural item, an uncountable amount, and one negative.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Neighborhood map:</b> Introduce three places on a fictional map, then ask the teacher three <span class="ex">Is there / Are there...?</span> questions about a second map.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Accessible room check:</b> Use a written room inventory or teacher-read scene. Report one available feature, two plural features, and one missing feature.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Choose an apartment:</b> Call about a fictional listing. Ask focused questions about bedrooms, transportation, stores, furniture, and one accessibility feature.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Introduce, then locate:</b> Introduce a place with <span class="ex">there is</span>, then refer to the known place with <span class="ex">it</span>: <span class="ex">There's a café on Pine Street. It's beside the library.</span></div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: recommend one neighborhood</h3>
    <p>Study two short fictional neighborhood inventories. Give a 45- to 60-second recommendation for one person: a commuter, a wheelchair user, or someone who enjoys cooking at home.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Introduce at least one singular place and one plural set of places.</li>
      <li>Include one uncountable amount or service, such as traffic, parking, or public transportation.</li>
      <li>State one missing feature with <span class="ex">isn't / aren't any</span> or <span class="ex">no</span>.</li>
      <li>Ask one correctly ordered <span class="ex">Is there...?</span> or <span class="ex">Are there...?</span> question.</li>
      <li>Refer back to one introduced place with <span class="ex">it</span> or <span class="ex">the + noun</span>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The teacher asks one follow-up question. Repair one sentence if the noun number, information status, or quantity word is unclear.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “One thing or an amount: there ______. More than one: there ______. In a question, ______ moves before there. In negatives and questions, plural nouns often take ______.”</p>
    <p>Then introduce three fictional things: one singular, one plural, and one uncountable amount. Refer back to one of them with <span class="ex">it</span> or <span class="ex">the + noun</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You matched form to noun number and quantity, built questions and short answers, and distinguished introducing new information from referring back to it.">
    <h3>Final quiz: there is / there are forms and meaning</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="There is" data-hint="The room inventory introduces one table for the first time." data-fix="There is a table in the kitchen.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. A room inventory introduces one table: ___ a table in the kitchen.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There is">There is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There are">There are</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It is">It is</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Are there" data-hint="Windows is plural, and the visitor is asking a question." data-fix="Are there any windows in the meeting room?">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. A visitor asks about plural windows in the meeting room: ___ any windows?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Are there">Are there</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Is there">Is there</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There are">There are</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="aren’t" data-hint="Buses is plural, and the schedule shows zero service at night." data-fix="There aren't any buses at night.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The schedule shows zero nighttime bus service: There ___ any buses at night.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="aren’t">aren’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="isn’t">isn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="not">not</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is" data-hint="Water is an uncountable amount here, so use is." data-fix="There is some water on the floor.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. A maintenance report introduces an uncountable amount: There ___ some water on the floor.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="be">be</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="There’s" data-hint="The guide is introducing one café, so use the contracted singular structure." data-fix="There's a good café near here.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. A local guide introduces one café for the first time: ___ a good café near here.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There’s">There’s</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It’s">It’s</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Is">Is</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="There’s a message for you." data-hint="The caller cannot see the message and does not know about it yet, so the receptionist must introduce it." data-fix="There's a message for you introduces the message before giving more details.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. A receptionist tells a caller about a message the caller cannot see and does not know about. Which sentence introduces the message?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There’s a message for you.">There’s a message for you.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The message is for you.">The message is for you.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It is for you.">It is for you.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="there is" data-hint="A positive short answer repeats there and the singular verb is, but not the noun." data-fix="Is there a pharmacy nearby? Yes, there is.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. Complete the positive short answer: “Is there a pharmacy nearby?” “Yes, ___.”</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="there is">there is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="it is">it is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="there’s a">there’s a</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Are there any seats?" data-hint="Seats is plural, so the question begins Are there and commonly uses any." data-fix="Are there any seats?">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. You want to know whether a waiting room has seats available. Which plural question is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Are there any seats?">Are there any seats?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Is there any seats?">Is there any seats?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="There are any seats?">There are any seats?</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Return tomorrow before rereading the lesson. Complete the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute next-day retrieval</a>, then revisit only the noun-number, quantity, question-order, or new-versus-known decision that still feels slow.</p>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day there is and there are retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved singular and plural introductions, a singular question, and a known-place reference without rereading the lesson.">
      <h3>Choose from number and information status</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Next-day existence and reference choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There is">There is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There are">There are</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Is there">Is there</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It is">It is</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The directory introduces one pharmacy: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="There is" data-hint="A pharmacy is one new countable thing, so use There is." data-fix="There is a pharmacy on Cedar Street." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a pharmacy on Cedar Street.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The directory introduces two clinics: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="There are" data-hint="Two clinics is plural, so use There are." data-fix="There are two clinics near the station." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> two clinics near the station.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A visitor asks about one accessible entrance: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Is there" data-hint="An accessible entrance is singular, and the visitor is asking a question." data-fix="Is there an accessible entrance?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> an accessible entrance?</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The pharmacy is now known. Refer back to it: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It is" data-hint="The pharmacy was already introduced, so refer back to that known place with It." data-fix="It is beside the library." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> beside the library.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="is" data-hint="Look ahead to the plural noun two elevators." data-fix="There are two elevators in the building." data-why="Two elevators is plural, so the introducing structure requires there are.">
      <h3>Repair the agreement</h3>
      <p>The building guide says “There is two elevators in the building.” Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
      <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="there">There</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="elevators">elevators</button></div>
      <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Thirty-second retrieval</h3>
      <p>Without looking back, introduce one café and two stores on an invented street. Ask whether there is a bank. Then refer back to the café with <span class="ex">it</span>.</p>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
      <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There's a café and there are two stores on the street. Is there a bank? The café is beside the station. It's open until 8.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>
